public@metalive.net (metalive) writes:

> I'm afraid I screwed up the last (4th) level of Sokoban. I'm missing
> only one more boulder to fill the last remaining hole... but it's in a
> corner :-(

There's a way to get it out of the corner without luck penalty.  
Just sit and think a little.  

> Here they are (if you guys don't mind nOObs like me):

If you read the FAQ, you're welcome to ask.  Sometimes 
groups.google.com will be a faster way, anyhow.  

> 1. If I risk reading a scroll or quaffing a potion I usually instantly
> notice some effect (allthough often I don't know what the vague
> description message of what just happened actually triggered). But
> let's say a certain scroll makes my hands glow red. Then I would want
> to name it for example "scroll of red glowing hands", in order that my
> custom name replaces the cryptic YUM YUM DWARA DEIDA BLA BLA crap. But
> how can I name a scroll or potion, that has just dissappered after
> use?

Let me introduce you to a great concept, 
called "making notes" ;-).  

> 2. Does worn armor "weigh" something?
> 
> 3. Does gold "weigh" something?

Yes, yes.

> 4. How can one repair corroded items?

Has to do something with enchant armor.  Read 
the spoilers if you must know.  Most armor, however, 
is better thrown away when corroded; you'll find 
better replacements for it.  

> 5. How does one remove cursed armor or rings, etc.?

You don't.  The point is not to put them on in the 
first place.  There is no way to remove a cursed 
item; there are, however, ways to uncurse an item, 
and ways to destroy worn items.  

> 6. Have those occaisional "dark" rooms any special meaning?

Maybe the dungeon supplies service center was short 
of torches.  Nothing to worry.  

> 7. How does one dig whole into the ground with pick-axes?

Just dig in the appropriate direction.  It might take 
more than one try.  

> 8. I think there is a strong lack of scrolls of identify in the game.

There are other means of identifying stuff.  However, 
this lack is apparent only at the beginning, and is, 
imo, a feature adding to the gaming delight.  You 
might wish to experiment a little (in explore mode) 
with blessed scrolls of identify if you need more 
id'ing power.  

